# Changelog (entries from newest to oldest): 

2026-10-27 David Chelidze

	Added Analysis 2 for counting warm summer days in Lund.

	* Added Analysis2.h and Analysis2.cxx.
	* Counted June-August days where the highest available daily temperature reaches the chosen threshold.
	* Excluded years with incomplete summer data.
	* Added a ROOT macro and PDF plot for Analysis 2.
	* Updated main.cxx and the Makefile to include Analysis 2.

2026-10-27 Estrella González Gómez <es2670go-s@student.lu.se>

	Installed the external CSV parser dependency and successfully built and ran the project

	* Cloned fast-cpp-csv-parser into external/include/csv to provide the csv/csv.h header required by DataExtraction.cxx. The dependency is installed locally and is not intended to be committed to the main repository.
	* Ran ParseData.py to generate datasets/ParsedData.csv from datasets/Data.csv, retaining observations with quality 'G' and extracting year, month, day, hour and temperature.
	* Successfully compiled the project using make.
	* Executed ./main, which generated temperature_tree.root containing the extracted observations in a ROOT TTree.

2026-10-25 Joel Johansen  <jo6312jo-s@student.lu.se>

	Fixed some syntax errors in the data extraction files and added a default constructor
	for the Observation class. Implemented the compilation of 
	the custom class Observation in Makefile using rootcling. Updated rootlogon.C

	* Debugged the src/Observation.cxx and include/Observation.h files and added a default 
	constructor for the class to ensure I/O compability
	* Using rootcling the Makefile was updated so that the custom class dictonary can be generated 
	using make. Added the Linkdef.h file needed for this. Also added the object files DataExtraction.o,
	Observation.o as well as ObservationDict.cxx so that the main executable can be built
	* Removed unused code from rootlogon.C and also added code so that libObservation.so is automatically loaded when a ROOT session is initialized
	* Running make libObservation.so followed by make main now creates an executable called main
	that generates a TTree 

2026-10-22 Joel Johansen  <jo6312jo-s@student.lu.se>

	Created the files needed for data extraction and a python script
	that parses the raw data

	* Created include/DataExtraction.h, include/Observation.h
	* Created src/DataExtraction.cxx, src/Observation.cxx
	* Added the Observation class to include/Observation.h, derived from the TObject class, with the 
	private members _year, _month, _day, _hour and _temperature. Also added 
	getters and setters and implemented all definitions of these in src/Observation.cxx
	* Added the functions parse_observation(csv_file) and write_observation(observations, tree_file) to
	include/DataExtraction.h. The first takes as input a .csv file and returns a vector of Observation objects. The second takes as input a vector of Observation objects and a .root filename and returns
	a TTree object with name "tree_file.root". The functions were implemented in src/DataExtraction.cxx
	* Wrote the ParseData.py script which parses the raw data and writes it to a new file

2026-10-20 Joel Johansen  <jo6312jo-s@student.lu.se>

	Updated the Workplan.md file 

	* Made a skeleton for a flowchart using mermaid 

